    "https://newhaven.hrmdirect.com/employment/job-opening.php?req=3755968&&#job": {
      "title": "Admissions Support Representative",
      "description": "Admissions Support Representative at University of New Haven Skip to jobs Back to Job Openings Admissions Support Representative Job Location West Haven, CT, US Apply Share Link copied Admissions Support Representative Who we are: The University of New Haven, founded on the Yale campus in 1920, is a private, coeducational university that has been recognized by The Princeton Review and U.S. News & World Report for academic excellence. Located between New York City and Boston in the shoreline city of West Haven, the University is a diverse and vibrant community of nearly 9,000 students from across the globe. Within its five colleges, students immerse themselves in a transformative, career-focused education across the liberal arts and sciences, fine arts, business, engineering, public safety and public service. More than 100 academic programs are offered, all grounded in a long-standing commitment to collaborative, interdisciplinary, project-based learning The Admissions Support Representative is an integral member of the Office of Admissions, providing exceptional customer service while supporting the daily operations of the admissions office. As one of the first points of contact for prospective students, families, school counselors, and campus visitors, this position helps create a welcoming and engaging experience that reflects the University's commitment to student success. The Admissions Support Representative coordinates campus visit operations, supports recruitment initiatives, assists with the planning and execution of admissions events, and contributes to achieving the University's enrollment goals. You will: Serve as the primary front desk representative, welcoming campus visitors and ensuring a professional, friendly, and organized check-in experience for prospective students, families, school counselors, and guests. Manage the main admissions phone line, responding to inquiries with exceptional customer service and directing calls to the appropriate staff as needed. Communicate with prospective students, families, and school counselors via phone, email, text, and in person, providing timely, accurate, and personalized information about the admissions process and the University. Coordinate daily campus visit logistics, including confirming visit registrations, preparing visit materials, and ensuring prospective students and guests have a seamless and engaging campus experience. Collaborate with student ambassadors and campus tour guides to coordinate daily schedules, maintain adequate tour coverage, and support a high-quality visitor experience. Conduct on-campus information sessions for prospective students and families, effectively communicating admissions information, academic opportunities, and campus resources. Create, maintain, and manage daily admissions staff and visitor coverage schedules to ensure efficient front desk operations and successful campus visit programming. Assist with application review and processing during peak admissions periods, as needed. Assist in the planning, coordination, and execution of admissions recruitment events, including Open Houses, Explore Days, Accepted Student programs, counselor events, and other on- and off-campus recruitment initiatives. Support event logistics, registration, setup, execution, and post-event follow-up to ensure successful programs and a positive guest experience. Collaborate with admissions staff and campus partners to continuously enhance visitor experiences and improve admissions operations and event effectiveness. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the mission of the University and the achievement of institutional enrollment goals. You need: Bachelor's degree required; and a minimum of 1 year of admission experience preferred. Proven customer service skills and minimum of 1 year of experience. Ability to represent the University of New Haven in a variety of situations and be able to competently interact with a diverse population of prospective students, faculty, and staff. Excellent interpersonal, organizational, and written communication skills. Proficiency in Microsoft suite of products required; Slate CRM system experience preferred. Willingness to work evening and weekends when required. Ability to lift up to 50 pounds is required for the travel component of the position. Must demonstrate a tireless commitment to enrolling and retaining a diverse student body. What’s In It for You: Health & Welfare Programs: Employees and their eligible family members, including spouses and dependent are eligible for Medical, Dental, Vision and Life Programs. Wellness & Fitness: On-campus Recreation and Fitness Center for employees and families; Employee Assistant Program Commitment to Educational Excellence: Tuition assistance for employees and eligible dependents; Tuition exchange opportunities Employee Discounts on products, services and educational opportunities Work/Life Benefits: Generous paid time off programs; progressive paid holiday schedule (including holiday break between Christmas and New Year’s); 4 weeks of parental paid leave; flexible work schedules including summer hours where applicable *The University of New Haven is not a qualifying E-Verify employer and its use of E-Verify is limited to specific government projects. For that reason, candidates with STEM OPT authorization cannot be considered for employment. © 2026 University of New Haven | Visit our home page Applicant tracking system powered by Powered by"
